    "https://www.notredame.edu.au/about-us/jobs-at-unda/employment-opportunities/job-details/_nocache?jobid=ofYWAfwt": {
      "title": "Payroll Compliance P&C Lead",
      "description": "Connect on social media Connect with Notre Dame on Social Media Australia LinkedIn X YouTube TikTok Fremantle Facebook Instagram Broome Facebook Instagram Sydney Facebook Instagram Payroll Compliance P&C Lead APPLY How to Apply Position Description Need help? Ask Notre Dame For further information or enquiries, please contact People and Culture: jobs@nd.edu.au Employment Type Full-Time Category Administrative Location Australia Department Finance Share LinkedIn Facebook X Email Payroll Compliance P&C Lead Payroll Compliance P&C Lead, Finance Sydney (Broadway) or Fremantle Campus Full time opportunity, F ixed T erm contract to Dec 2027 Rewarding Opportunity Friendly and collaborative environment Level 8 + 15% superannuation About the university We believe in the power of education to transform lives, strengthen communities and help people become the best version of themselves. The University of Notre Dame Australia is a modern, national Catholic university that serves more than 12,000 students across its campuses in Fremantle, Broome and Sydney. With a community of over 1,000 academic and professional staff, Notre Dame is recognised for its personalised learning environment, strong graduate outcomes and holistic educational philosophy rooted in critical thinking, ethics and the Catholic intellectual tradition. About the office A newly established Project Team dedicated to strengthening payroll compliance, enhancing governance, and driving best practice across the University. About the role Th is role provides specialist People & Culture expertise to support payroll compliance . Acting as the key liaison between the Payroll Compliance Team and P&C, the role ensures workforce data is accurately interpreted, validated and applied to compliance activities. The position requires strong P&C and payroll knowledge, systems proficiency, sound judgement and effective stakeholder collaboration to support employment compliance and risk management in a complex, sensitive and time-critical environment. Key Responsibilities Provide People & Culture advice and support to support p ayroll compliance . Review policies and procedures for compliance and recommend process improvements. Validate employment, classification and payroll data in PeopleSoft and other systems. Identify and escalate data discrepancies, risks and compliance issues. L iaise w ith current and former employees to obtain information regarding conditions and historical matters, as required. Coordinate input across HR, Payroll, Finance and other stakeholders. Maintain accurate records to ensure auditability and reliable project outcomes. Qualifications, skills & experience Relevant qualifications in HR, business, information systems or equivalent experience and training. Experience in People & Culture, HR operations or HR systems. Strong working knowledge of PeopleSoft and the ability to validate employee, position, employment and payroll data. Strong u nderstanding of payroll processes, employment records and HR systems. Experience in data analysis, compliance, audits or project support. Ability to navigate SharePoint, corporate drives, HRIS and other systems. Strong investigative, analytical and problem-solving skills, with attention to detail and the ability to work independently. Excellent written and verbal communication skills to explain complex information clearly. How to apply Please apply online with a resume and cover letter outlining your suitability for the role. Applications closing date: 29 October 202 6 For further information on how to apply, please visit: How to apply | Notre Dame Applicants are expected to have current and valid work rights in Australia. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people are encouraged to apply. The University of Notre Dame Australia seeks to increase the diversity of our workforce to better meet the different needs of the University and its stakeholders and to improve equal opportunity outcomes for our staff. The University is committed to providing a safe, respectful and inclusive working and learning environment. The successful candidate will be required to complete a self-declaration regarding Gender-Based Violence (as required by the National Code) as part of the pre-employment process. For more information on this please refer to our website. Contact us Please direct your queries regarding this role to Janette Tam, janette.tam@nd.edu.au Unsolicited contact from recruitment agencies will not be entertained. Back to current openings"
    },
    "https://www.notredame.edu.au/about-us/jobs-at-unda/employment-opportunities/job-details/_nocache?jobid=oeNRAfwc": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer (Discipline Lead GP Supervisors, CPD, Quality & Curriculum Interface), School of Medicine",
      "description": "Connect on social media Connect with Notre Dame on Social Media Australia LinkedIn X YouTube TikTok Fremantle Facebook Instagram Broome Facebook Instagram Sydney Facebook Instagram Senior Lecturer (Discipline Lead GP Supervisors, CPD, Quality & Curriculum Interface), School of Medicine APPLY How to Apply Position Description Need help? Ask Notre Dame For further information or enquiries, please contact People and Culture: jobs@nd.edu.au Employment Type Part-Time Category Medicine Location Sydney Department School of Medicine Share LinkedIn Facebook X Email Senior Lecturer (Discipline Lead GP Supervisors, CPD, Quality & Curriculum Interface), School of Medicine Senior Lecturer (Discipline Lead GP Supervisors, CPD, Quality & Curriculum Interface), School of Medicine Sydney (Darlinghurst) Campus Part-time opportunity (0. 2 ), Continuing contract Friendly and collaborative work environment Rewarding opportunity offering career development Level C from $147,864 + 15.00% superannuation About the university We believe in the power of education to transform lives, strengthen communities and help people become the best version of themselves. The University of Notre Dame Australia is a modern, national Catholic university that serves more than 12,000 students across its campuses in Fremantle, Broome and Sydney. With a community of over 1,000 academic and professional staff, Notre Dame is recognised for its personalised learning environment, strong graduate outcomes and holistic educational philosophy rooted in critical thinking, ethics and the Catholic intellectual tradition. About the role Reporting to the Head of Discipline, General Practice, you will provide leadership to GP clinical supervision across the MD program. You will oversee supervisor recruitment, support and engagement, build strong stakeholder relationships, and ensure quality teaching and curriculum delivery . Key Responsibilities Recruit, onboard, and retain GP and community-based clinical placements to support high-quality student learning. Support and mentor GP Clinical Supervisors, building confidence, capability, and engagement in teaching. Coordinate and deliver supervisor development programs aligned with CPD and accreditation requirements. Foster strong relationships with GP supervisors and practices through regular engagement, communication, and site visits. Monitor and enhance teaching quality through feedback, issue resolution, and quality assurance processes. Support delivery of the General Practice curriculum across Years 1–4, ensuring alignment with learning outcomes. Contribute to educational evaluation, scholarship, and research in General Practice teaching and supervision. Qualifications, skills & experience You will have advanced qualifications and re cognised significant experience in the relevant discipline area. A position at this level will normally require a doctoral qualification or equivalent accreditation and standing. Possession of medical qualification registrable with AHPRA and a Fellowship of the Royal Australian College of General Practitioners (FRACGP) is essential . A PhD qualification is desirable . Demonstrated experience in teaching at Masters level or higher, or in medical, health or professional practice-based education settings . Demonstrated active engagement and track record in medical education. Experience in curriculum design, delivery and evaluation. Experience teaching medical students and/or supervisors across multiple stages of training. Strong understanding of accreditation requirements and contemporary medical education principles. Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively across multiple stakeholder groups. Demonstrated leadership experience within a higher education, healthcare, or educational institution. Background in quality assurance and continuous improvement. Exposure to medical education research and evaluation. Knowledge of General Practice and medical education. Understanding of accreditation and quality standards. Excellent communication and teamwork skills. Benefits Fitness Passport on offer. Generous training and development opportunities. Friendly and collaborative working environment. How to apply Please apply online with a resume and cover letter outlining your suitability for the role. Applications closing date: 29 October 2026 For further information on how to apply, please visit: How to apply | Notre Dame Applicants are expected to have current and valid work rights in Australia. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people are encouraged to apply. The University is committed to providing a safe, respectful and inclusive working and learning environment. The successful candidate will be required to complete a self-declaration regarding Gender-Based Violence (as required by the National Code) as part of the pre-employment process. For more information on this please refer to our website. The University of Notre Dame Australia seeks to increase the diversity of our workforce to better meet the different needs of the University and its stakeholders and to improve equal opportunity outcomes for our staff. Contact us Please direct your queries regarding this role to Melissa Schmidt , Melissa.schmidt@nd.edu.au Unsolicited contact from recruitment agencies will not be entertained. Back to current openings"
    },
    "https://www.notredame.edu.au/about-us/jobs-at-unda/employment-opportunities/job-details/_nocache?jobid=oWmXAfwz": {
      "title": "EOI - Academic Sessional, Pathways Program",
      "description": "Connect on social media Connect with Notre Dame on Social Media Australia LinkedIn X YouTube TikTok Fremantle Facebook Instagram Broome Facebook Instagram Sydney Facebook Instagram EOI - Academic Sessional, Pathways Program APPLY How to Apply Need help? Ask Notre Dame For further information or enquiries, please contact People and Culture: jobs@nd.edu.au Employment Type Sessional Category Casual/ Sessional Location Fremantle Department Study Centre Share LinkedIn Facebook X Email EOI - Academic Sessional, Pathways Program EOI - Academic Sessional, Pathways Tertiary Pathway Program and UniPath in Schools Fremantle or Sydney Campus Rewarding opportunity Friendly and collaborative environment Ongoing learning and professional development opportunities About the university We believe in the power of education to transform lives, strengthen communities and help people become the best version of themselves. The University of Notre Dame Australia is a modern, national Catholic university that serves more than 12,000 students across its campuses in Fremantle, Broome and Sydney. With a community of over 1,000 academic and professional staff, Notre Dame is recognised for its personalised learning environment, strong graduate outcomes and holistic educational philosophy rooted in critical thinking, ethics and the Catholic intellectual tradition . About the office About Pathways · Tertiary Pathway Program · UniPath in Schools About the role The School seeks expressions of interest from academics who have a passion for teaching. Teaching opportunities are available on a sessional basis in the Tertiary Pathway Program (TPP). We are looking for sessional academic tutors with subject matter expertise in at least one or more of the following areas: Essential Maths (Fremantle) Research Skills (Fremantle) Academic Writing (Broadway, Sydney) Human Biology ( Broadway,Sydney ) Key Responsibilities Conduct teaching to the standard of the Pathways programs. This includes preparation for the tutorials and facilitating discussions to enhance student engagement. Consultation with students in relation to pre-tutorial tasks, weekly topics and upcoming assessments. Participating in assessment activities, including marking, moderation and providing feedback to students within the prescribed timeframes. Comply with policies and procedures in all aspects of their work and conduct, in particular the Staff Code of Conduct. Undertake Professional Development as arranged by the National Director of the Program. Provision of a high level of pastoral care to students. Qualifications, skills & experience Supportive of the Objects of Notre Dame as a Catholic University. A Master’s degree and experience in Teaching in university pathway programs (preferably experience in enabling programs and first year courses) . Ability to teach small tutorial groups and engage students in their learning. Ability to deliver quality learning and teaching practices in multiple modes including online delivery. A keen interest in maintaining currency in scholarship and professional practice. Ability to incorporate technology (e.g. Blackboard, Teams, email, internet) into teaching and learning. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills, including ability to work effectively in a team. Ability to assess priority of tasks, manage workload and meet deadlines in a busy education environment. Evidence of a high level of pastoral care to students. Benefits Generous training and development opportunities Friendly and collaborative working environment How to apply Please apply online with a resume and cover letter outlining your suitability for the role. For further information on how to apply, please visit: How to apply | Notre Dame Applicants are expected to have current and valid work rights in Australia. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people are encouraged to apply. The University is committed to providing a safe, respectful and inclusive working and learning environment. The successful candidate will be required to complete a self-declaration regarding Gender-Based Violence (as required by the National Code) as part of the pre-employment process. For more information on this please refer to our website. The University of Notre Dame Australia seeks to increase the diversity of our workforce to better meet the different needs of the University and its stakeholders and to improve equal opportunity outcomes for our staff. Contact us Please direct your queries regarding this role to Anita Zele, Anita.Zele@nd.edu.au Please quote the Job title and reference number in the subject line. Unsolicited contact from recruitment agencies will not be entertained. Back to current openings"
    },
    "https://www.notredame.edu.au/about-us/jobs-at-unda/employment-opportunities/job-details/_nocache?jobid=oPHPAfwF": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer, (Public Health Domain), School of Medicine",
      "description": "Connect on social media Connect with Notre Dame on Social Media Australia LinkedIn X YouTube TikTok Fremantle Facebook Instagram Broome Facebook Instagram Sydney Facebook Instagram Senior Lecturer, (Public Health Domain), School of Medicine APPLY How to Apply Position Description Need help? Ask Notre Dame For further information or enquiries, please contact People and Culture: jobs@nd.edu.au Employment Type Part-Time Category Medicine Location Sydney Department School of Medicine Share LinkedIn Facebook X Email Senior Lecturer, (Public Health Domain), School of Medicine Senior Lecturer (Public Health) , School of Medicine Sydney Campus Part-time opportunity (0. 5 ) , Continuing contract Friendly and collaborative work environment Rewarding opportunity offering career developmen t Level C from $147,864 + 1 5 . 0 0% super annuation About the university We believe in the power of education to transform lives, strengthen communities and help people become the best version of themselves. The University of Notre Dame Australia is a modern, national Catholic university that serves more than 12,000 students across its campuses in Fremantle, Broome and Sydney. With a community of over 1,000 academic and professional staff, Notre Dame is recognised for its personalised learning environment, strong graduate outcomes and holistic educational philosophy rooted in critical thinking, ethics and the Catholic intellectual tradition. About the role The Public Health Domain is one of six domains within the Doctor of Medicine program, delivered across Sydney, Fremantle and Broome. Working as part of the public health team, you will contribute to the delivery of public health education, research, epidemiological health assessment, and curriculum development within t he Medicine program . The focus is on p opulation health, equity, the social determinants including environmental determinant s of health, evidence- inform ed practice, and the provision of sustainable healthcare to protect and promote the health of populations . Key Responsibilities Integrate Public Health learning across the MD program. Develop and deliver a contemporary Public Health curriculum and learning activities. Support the recruitment, training, mentoring and coordination of tutors and sessional staff . Collaborate with clinical, academic and community partners to deliver teaching aligned with learning outcomes and community priorities . Coordinate immersi ve learning activities and intersectoral, interdisciplinary initiatives. Contribute to the design , deliver y and marking of student assess ments of learning in Public Health. Deliver high-quality teaching and promote public health education and student engagement . Contribute to evaluation, research, scholarship and quality improvement in medical education and the Public Health Domain . Represent the Public Health Domain on committees and University initiatives as required. Qualifications, skills & experience Possession of a medical qualification registrable with AHPRA and a Fellowship of a relevant professional body, preferably Fellow of the Australasian Faculty of Public Health Medicine, OR a qualified health professional with a PhD in an area relevant to public health and medical education with more than 5 years teaching in a tertiary education context. Master of Public Health or equivalent post-graduate degree in a relevant field. Experience in teaching at Masters level or higher or in medical, health or professional practice-based education settings. Excellent written and verbal communication and stakeholder engagement skills. Demonstrated understanding of the Australian healthcare system and delivery of public health ser vic es in metropolitan, regional and rural communities . Demonstrated c ommitment to public health, public health education, environmental sustainability , research and scholarship. Experience in teaching, facilitation and student support. Ability to work intersectorally to develop and maintain mutually benefic ial relation ships with external institutions and partners (government, non-government and community-controlled) across the public health sector . Ability to work independently and collaboratively. Strong digital literacy and proficiency with learning technologies. Benefits Fitness Passport on offer . Generous training and development opportunities. Friendly and collaborative working environment. How to apply Please apply online with a resume and cover letter outlining your suitability for the role. Applications closing date: 3 November 2026 For further information on how to apply, please visit: How to apply | Notre Dame Applicants are expected to have current and valid work rights in Australia. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people are encouraged to apply. The University is committed to providing a safe, respectful and inclusive working and learning environment. The successful candidate will be required to complete a self-declaration regarding Gender-Based Violence (as required by the National Code) as part of the pre-employment process. For more information on this please refer to our website. The University of Notre Dame Australia seeks to increase the diversity of our workforce to better meet the different needs of the University and its stakeholders and to improve equal opportunity outcomes for our staff. Contact us Please direct your queries regarding this role to Melissa Schmidt , Melissa.schmidt@nd.edu.au Unsolicited contact from recruitment agencies will not be entertained. Back to current openings"
    },
    "https://www.notredame.edu.au/about-us/jobs-at-unda/employment-opportunities/job-details/_nocache?jobid=oNZOAfwU": {
      "title": "Lecturer (Clinical Education, Physiotherapy), School of Health Sciences",
      "description": "Connect on social media Connect with Notre Dame on Social Media Australia LinkedIn X YouTube TikTok Fremantle Facebook Instagram Broome Facebook Instagram Sydney Facebook Instagram Lecturer (Clinical Education, Physiotherapy), School of Health Sciences APPLY How to Apply Position Description Need help? Ask Notre Dame For further information or enquiries, please contact People and Culture: jobs@nd.edu.au Employment Type Full-Time Category Education & Training Location Sydney Department School of Health Sciences Share LinkedIn Facebook X Email Lecturer (Clinical Education, Physiotherapy), School of Health Sciences Lecturer (Clinical Education Physiotherapy) , School of Health Sciences Sydney (Broadway) Campus Full-time opportunity, Continuing c ontract (FTE negotiable for a successful candidate) Fast paced environment with opportunity for professional growth Friendly and collaborative working environment From $ 121,739 pa (level B) + 1 5 % superannuation About the university We believe in the power of education to transform lives, strengthen communities and help people become the best version of themselves. The University of Notre Dame Australia is a modern, national Catholic university that serves more than 12,000 students across its campuses in Fremantle, Broome and Sydney. With a community of over 1,000 academic and professional staff, Notre Dame is recognised for its personalised learning environment, strong graduate outcomes and holistic educational philosophy rooted in critical thinking, ethics and the Catholic intellectual tradition . About the school The School of Health Sciences offers an extensive range of quality accredited undergraduate and postgraduate programs designed to engage students from learning opportunities in class through to professional workplace experience . About the role The School of Health Sciences is seeking to appoint a dedicated and experienced physiotherapist to join our Clinical Education Team. While this is a multidisciplinary team, the role will primarily focus on supporting the Master of Physiotherapy program. This position offers the opportunity to contribute to clinical education and, where appropriate, other areas of teaching aligned with your academic and professional expertise. Expertise in cardiorespiratory, paediatric or neurological physiotherapy would be highly regarded. Key Responsibilities Provide on-site support to enhance the clinical supervision and education skills of clinical education personnel. Advise students and participate in marking and assessment processes related to their preparation for clinical placements. Contribute to the development and maintenance of high standards in clinical education through quality improvement initiatives. Liaise and negotiate with clinical education providers across New South Wales, government, non-government, private sectors, and other universities. Assist in developing and expanding clinical placement opportunities for undergraduate students, including rural, remote, and multidisciplinary settings. Offer pastoral care and consultation to support student wellbeing throughout their clinical education experience. Qualifications, skills & experience A higher degree or equivalent clinical professional experience with recognised standing in the discipline of physiotherapy. Current, full registration as a physiotherapist with the Physiotherapists Registration Board under AHPRA. Significant and relevant clinical experience, with a strong understanding of clinical facilities, systems and culture in New South Wales. Demonstrated experience in clinical education and student placements, supported by excellent administrative and organisational skills. Strong oral and written communication skills, with the ability to work collaboratively and lead within a team environment. Benefits Fast paced environment with opportunity for professional growth Generous training and development opportunities Friendly and collaborative working environment How to apply Please apply online with a resume and a brief cover letter outlining your suitability for the role. Applications closing date: 3 November 2026 For further information on how to apply, please visit: How to apply | Notre Dame Applicants are expected to have current and valid work rights in Australia. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people are encouraged to apply. The University is committed to providing a safe, respectful and inclusive working and learning environment. The successful candidate will be required to complete a self-declaration regarding Gender-Based Violence (as required by the National Code) as part of the pre-employment process. For more information on this please refer to our website. The University of Notre Dame Australia seeks to increase the diversity of our workforce to better meet the different needs of the University and its stakeholders and to improve equal opportunity outcomes for our staff. Contact us Please direct your queries regarding this role to Janelle Gill, National Director of Clinical Education Janelle.Gill@nd.edu.au Unsolicited contact from recruitment agencies will not be entertained. Back to current openings"
    },
    "https://www.notredame.edu.au/about-us/jobs-at-unda/employment-opportunities/job-details/_nocache?jobid=oomWAfw0": {
      "title": "EOI - Tertiary Supervisors of School and/or Early Childhood Education Centre Placements",
      "description": "Connect on social media Connect with Notre Dame on Social Media Australia LinkedIn X YouTube TikTok Fremantle Facebook Instagram Broome Facebook Instagram Sydney Facebook Instagram EOI - Tertiary Supervisors of School and/or Early Childhood Education Centre Placements APPLY How to Apply Need help? Ask Notre Dame For further information or enquiries, please contact People and Culture: jobs@nd.edu.au Employment Type Sessional Category Casual/ Sessional Location Australia Department School of Education Share LinkedIn Facebook X Email EOI - Tertiary Supervisors of School and/or Early Childhood Education Centre Placements EOI – Tertiary Supervisors of School and/or Early Childhood Education Centre Placements School of Education Fremantle & Sydney Campus , some regional and r ural opportunities Rewarding opportunity Friendly and collaborative environment Ongoing learning and professional development opportunities About the university The University of Notre Dame Australia is a Catholic University with over 1,000 permanent staff providing an exceptional educational experience to over 12,000 students across our Fremantle, Broome, and Sydney campuses, as well as clinical schools in Victoria an d New South Wales. About the school The School of Education aims to develop passionate, profession-ready teachers who are highly valued in a range of settings. Whether our graduates choose to work in early childhood, primary or secondary education, we recognise that teaching is more than a profession – it is a vocation. With the support of our leading educators, they will develop the skills to lead and inspire future generations. About the role The School of Education seeks expressions of interest from experienced Primary, Secondary and Early Childhood teachers who have a passion for teaching. We are seeking tertiary supervisors who will observe pre-service teachers facilitate lessons/experiences and meet with them in the schools/centres during their P rofessional E xperience placements. Key activities for this role include: s upervising, observing and supporting preservice teachers, assessing their progress in relation to the Australian Professional Standards for Teachers and liaising with mentor teachers and other school/centre staff. This oppor tunity may be suitable for those we have recently retired from teaching, are taking a career break or currently work part time in schools . Key Responsibilities Supervise the preservice teacher throughout their Professional Experience placement. Supervision includes: - Lesson/experience observations, - W ritten feedback to the pre-service teacher, - C ollaborative discussions with the mentor teacher and pre-service teacher Act as an independent advocate for the pre - service teacher, supporting all aspects of the placement. Demonstrate knowledge and understanding of The Australian Professional Standards for Teachers and make judgements about the extent to which preservice teachers meet the Standards. Demonstrate understanding of the Core Curriculum requirements in the Strong Beginnings Report . Make initial phone and/or email contact and conduct face-to-face school/centre visits throughout the placement period. Qualifications, skills & experience A teaching qualification in Early Childhood , Primary and/or Secondary teaching, minimum 5 years of teaching experience and a current Working With Children Check . Proven capacity to support the professional growth of others through mentoring and meaningful feedback. Demonstrated ability to establish and maintain effective professional relationships with pre-service teachers, school teachers and school/centre staff, including the confidence to address concerns and engage in challenging professional discussions. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills, including ability to foster high levels of collegiality and ability to empathise with students , teachers and students/children . Proven ability to assess priority of tasks, manage workload and meet deadlines, in a busy education environment. Available to work during the school day for school/ early childhood services visits. Supportive of the Objects of Notre Dame as a Catholic University. Desirable: Current drivers licence and vehicle How to apply Please apply online with a CV and cover letter outlining your suitability for the role. For further information on how to apply, please visit: How to apply | Notre Dame Applicants are expected to have current and valid work rights in Australia. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people are encouraged to apply. The University of Notre Dame Australia seeks to increase the diversity of our workforce to better meet the different needs of the University and its stakeholders and to improve equal opportunity outcomes for our staff. Contact us Please direct your queries regarding this role to Joanne Giannini , National Lead, Professional Experience joanne.giannini1@nd.edu.au Unsolicited contact from recruitment agencies will not be entertained. Back to current openings"
    },
    "https://www.notredame.edu.au/about-us/jobs-at-unda/employment-opportunities/job-details/_nocache?jobid=ouqOAfw2": {
      "title": "National Practicum Placement Administration Coordinator, School of Health Sciences",
      "description": "Connect on social media Connect with Notre Dame on Social Media Australia LinkedIn X YouTube TikTok Fremantle Facebook Instagram Broome Facebook Instagram Sydney Facebook Instagram National Practicum Placement Administration Coordinator, School of Health Sciences APPLY How to Apply Position Description Need help? Ask Notre Dame For further information or enquiries, please contact People and Culture: jobs@nd.edu.au Employment Type Full-Time Category Administrative Location Australia Department School of Health Sciences Share LinkedIn Facebook X Email National Practicum Placement Administration Coordinator, School of Health Sciences National Practicum Placement Administration Coordinator , School of Health Sciences Sydney (Broadway) or Fremantle (WA) Campus Full-time opportunity, Continuing c ontract Friendly and collaborative environment Rewarding opportunity $ 95,096 pa (level 6 - Fremantle ) + 1 5 % superannuation $106,302 pa (level 6 - Sydney) + 15% superannuation About the university We believe in the power of education to transform lives, strengthen communities and help people become the best version of themselves. The University of Notre Dame Australia is a modern, national Catholic university that serves more than 12,000 students across its campuses in Fremantle, Broome and Sydney. With a community of over 1,000 academic and professional staff, Notre Dame is recognised for its personalised learning environment, strong graduate outcomes and holistic educational philosophy rooted in critical thinking, ethics and the Catholic intellectual tradition . About the office The School of Health Sciences offers an extensive range of quality accredited undergraduate and postgraduate programs designed to engage students from learning opportunities in class through to professional workplace experience. Our School is distinctive for its teaching culture, delivery of quality contemporary education and its pastoral care mission. About the role This role leads the national coordination and administration of student clinical and practicum placements across the School of Health Sciences, ensuring all placements meet course requirements, accreditation standards, contractual obligations, and university policies. Working closely with academic staff, professional teams, placement providers, and regulatory bodies, the position drives compliance, consistency, and continuous improvement across the University's national footprint. Key Responsibilities Lead the national administration of clinical and practicum placements, ensuring consistency, efficiency, compliance, and alignment with course requirements, accreditation standards, and university expectations. Provide leadership, guidance, and workload management for placement administration staff, including training, performance development, and fostering a high-performing, collaborative team culture. Build and maintain effective relationships with students, academic and professional staff, placement providers, regulatory bodies, and external partners to support successful placement outcomes. Oversee end-to-end placement administration, including placement requests, scheduling, onboarding, allocations, compliance monitoring, and maintenance of accurate records across placement management systems. Manage placement agreements, contracts, compliance requirements, and financial processes, including contract monitoring, cost projections, invoice reconciliation, and regulatory adherence. Drive continuous improvement through the development of national procedures, monitoring data quality, preparing reports, enhancing systems and processes, and supporting university committees and stakeholder initiatives. Qualifications, skills & experience A degree with relevant experience in administrative management; or extensive experience and demonstrated expertise in practicum placement coordination; or broad experience in administrative roles; or an equivalent combination of relevant experience and education/training. Demonstrated experience leading or supervising teams within complex environments, including task delegation, staff development, performance management, and fostering a collaborative, high-performing culture. Proven ability to coordinate complex administrative processes and systems, ideally within higher education, healthcare, or similarly regulated environments. Highly developed organisational, communication, and stakeholder engagement skills, with the ability to manage competing priorities, deadlines, and relationships across multiple locations. Strong analytical and administrative capabilities, including data management, reporting, financial administration, invoice processing, budget support, and maintaining a high level of accuracy and attention to detail. Proficiency in Microsoft Office and placement or student management systems (such as SONIA or InPlace ), with an understanding of contract management, service agreements, and compliance requirements associated with external partnerships. Benefits Fast paced environment with opportunity for professional growth Generous training and development opportunities Friendly and collaborative working environment How to apply Please apply online with a resume and cover letter outlining your suitability for the role. Applications closing date: 3 November 2026 For further information on how to apply, please visit: How to apply | Notre Dame Applicants are expected to have current and valid work rights in Australia. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people are encouraged to apply. The University is committed to providing a safe, respectful and inclusive working and learning environment. The successful candidate will be required to complete a self-declaration regarding Gender-Based Violence (as required by the National Code) as part of the pre-employment process. For more information on this please refer to our website. The University of Notre Dame Australia seeks to increase the diversity of our workforce to better meet the different needs of the University and its stakeholders and to improve equal opportunity outcomes for our staff. Contact us Please direct your queries regarding this role to Haritha Garlapati , Haritha.Garlapati@nd.edu.au Unsolicited contact from recruitment agencies will not be entertained. Back to current openings"
    },
    "https://www.notredame.edu.au/about-us/jobs-at-unda/employment-opportunities/job-details/_nocache?jobid=oWoOAfws": {
      "title": "EOI – National Deputy Head of School (Cross Disciplinary Strategy and Development) School of Education - Internal Only",
      "description": "Connect on social media Connect with Notre Dame on Social Media Australia LinkedIn X YouTube TikTok Fremantle Facebook Instagram Broome Facebook Instagram Sydney Facebook Instagram EOI – National Deputy Head of School (Cross Disciplinary Strategy and Development) School of Education - Internal Only APPLY How to Apply Position Description Need help? Ask Notre Dame For further information or enquiries, please contact People and Culture: jobs@nd.edu.au Employment Type Part-Time Category Teaching & Research Location Australia Department School of Education Share LinkedIn Facebook X Email EOI – National Deputy Head of School (Cross Disciplinary Strategy and Development) School of Education - Internal Only EOI – National Deputy Head of School ( Cross Disci plinary Strategy and Development), School of Education - Internal Only Sydney or Fremantle Campus – location will be dependent upon the successful applicant’s current location. Fixed Term Contract ( 31 July, 2028 ) , Part-time (0.6) Leadership Opportunity Friendly and collaborative environment Academic Level + DHoS allowance + superannuation About the role This position reports to the National Head of School and involves leadership in the National School of Education and ongoing support for the operations of the School , including teaching, research and service/engagement. Key Responsibilities Leadership of the implementation of the School’s courses and programs at the campus and nationally including contributing to quality assurance and achievement of targets. Leading work packages related to cross disciplinary strategy in teaching and research. Contribution to the performance of the School in relation to Learning & Teaching and Research. Support the financial management of the National School through relevant financial delegation. Co-supervision and management of school staff located on their campus in the context of University delegation, including supervision, workload and leave management. Key representational and leadership role of the school in a campus-based setting providing local responsiveness to and with campus-based Committees, external stakeholders and or industry partners. Training, and Community Engagement in the context of organisational and Faculty strategies. Qualifications, skills & experience This fixed term role relates to a specific need in response to recent federal government changes in the ways universities operate, the nature of changing student cohorts, and changing requirements for student attraction and retention. A Doctoral qualification and research track in a relevant discipline area or equivalent industry experience. Leadership experience as National Program or Discipline Coordinator or other formal leadership appointment in a university. Demonstrated capacity to develop a cross-disciplinary sciences focus in teaching and research in initial teacher education and/or post graduate education (e.g., STEM, STEAM, STREAM). Capacity to support the development of a school and/or faculty research agenda focused on ITE pedagogies. Understanding of budget and financial management principles and obligations to compliance with University targets. Demonstrated alignment with UNDA’s strategic pillars in connection with teacher education. Demonstrated commitment to the breadth of university life through Service and Leadership . How to apply Please apply online with a resume , including qualifications and recent experience, and a cover letter addressing the qualifications, skills and experiences. Applications closing date: COB Tuesday 3 November, 2026 For further information on how to apply, please visit: How to apply | Notre Dame Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people are encouraged to apply. The University of Notre Dame Australia seeks to increase the diversity of our workforce to better meet the different needs of the University and its stakeholders and to improve equal opportunity outcomes for our staff. Contact us Please direct your queries regarding this role to Janette Tam , janette.tam@nd.edu.au Back to current openings"
    },
