      "title": "EOI – National Deputy Head of School (Quality Teaching and Pedagogical Research), School of Education (Internal Only)",
      "description": "Connect on social media Connect with Notre Dame on Social Media Australia LinkedIn X YouTube TikTok Fremantle Facebook Instagram Broome Facebook Instagram Sydney Facebook Instagram EOI – National Deputy Head of School (Quality Teaching and Pedagogical Research), School of Education (Internal Only) APPLY How to Apply Position Description Need help? Ask Notre Dame For further information or enquiries, please contact People and Culture: jobs@nd.edu.au Employment Type Part-Time Category Education & Training Location Australia Department School of Education Share LinkedIn Facebook X Email EOI – National Deputy Head of School (Quality Teaching and Pedagogical Research), School of Education (Internal Only) EOI – National Deputy Head of School (Quality T eaching and Pedagogical Research ), School of Education - Internal Only Sydney or Fremantle Campus – location will be dependent upon the successful applicant’s current location. Fixed Term Contract ( 31 July, 2028 ) , Part-time (0.6) Leadership Opportunity Friendly and collaborative environment Academic Level + DHoS allowance + superannuation About the role This position reports to the National Head of School and involves leadership in the National School of Education and ongoing support for the operations of the School, including teaching, research and service/engagement. Key Responsibilities Leadership of the implementation of the School’s courses and programs at the campus and nationally including contributing to quality assurance and achievement of targets. Leading work packages related to quality teaching and pedagogical research. Contribution to the performance of the School in relation to Learning & Teaching and Research in consultation and partnership with the Deputy Head of School for Philosophy and Theology and Associate Dean Learning and Teaching (ADLT). Support the financial management of the National School through relevant financial delegation. Co-supervision and management of school staff located on their campus in the context of University delegation, including supervision, workload and leave management. Key representational and leadership role of the school in a campus-based setting providing local responsiveness to and with campus-based Committees, external stakeholders and or industry partners. Training, and Community Engagement in the context of organisational and Faculty strategies. Qualifications, skills & experience This fixed term role relates to a specific need in response to recent federal government changes in the ways universities operate, the nature of changing student cohorts, and changing requirements for student attraction and retention. A Doctoral qualification and research track in a relevant discipline area or equivalent industry experience. Leadership experience as National Program or Discipline Coordinator or similar level in a university setting. Demonstrated capacity to support quality teaching aligned with UNDA Learning and Teaching strategy and resources including Blackboard ultra, Cadmus, assessment design and academic integrity (including focus on Artificial Intelligence). Capacity to support the development of a school and/or faculty research agenda focused on ITE pedagogies. Understanding of budget and financial management principles and obligations to compliance with University targets. Demonstrated alignment with UNDA’s strategic pillars in connection with teacher education. Demonstrated commitment to the breadth of university life through Service and Leadership . How to apply Please apply online with a resume, including qualifications and recent experience, and a cover letter addressing the qualifications, skills and experiences. Applications closing date: COB Tuesday 3 November, 2026 For further information on how to apply, please visit: How to apply | Notre Dame Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people are encouraged to apply. The University of Notre Dame Australia seeks to increase the diversity of our workforce to better meet the different needs of the University and its stakeholders and to improve equal opportunity outcomes for our staff. Contact us Please direct your queries regarding this role to Janette Tam , janette.tam@nd.edu.au Back to current openings"
